ecomes two separate commands; token truncation at 63 bytes; the `MAX_ARGS` cap.\n- **NUL-truncated string views**: `status\\0extra` runs `status`; the tail is silently dropped.\n- Original error-check order, prompt-before-EOF trailing `> `, and `exit(0)` semantics preserved.\n\n## One judgement call worth flagging\n\nAn empty input line reads C's **uninitialised `command` buffer** — undefined behavior. The reference build (CMakeLists sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the compiler is unoptimised) always sees an empty buffer, making blank lines no-ops; I matched that. At `-O2`/`-O3` the stale previous command survives and gets re-executed instead. I documented this in the source so the dependency on build flags is explicit rather than silently baked in.\n\n`cargo build --release` and `cargo clippy` are both warning-free. Unsafe code is confined to the `time`/`ctime` FFI calls, which guarantee byte-identical timestamps including local-timezone handling; everything else is safe Rust."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":96271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c396d825-bd3f-4ee0-b910-db33faed22c4","uuid":"a93c0376-3f48-440e-a7d2-7a4fd026bd46","timestamp":"2026-08-28T05:36:42.583Z"}
